### Create API Key
# Generates a new API key for a client.
# The response includes the plain-text "key" ONLY ONCE - it cannot be retrieved
# later, only its hash is stored in the DB (see apiKey.KeyHash.Generate).
# Body fields:
#   client_id              (int)     ID of the client that owns the key
#   description            (string)  free text to identify the key later
#   environment            (string)  development | staging | production (used when generating the key)
#   rate_limit_per_minute  (int32)   rate limiter limit for this key
# Returns 201 with { message, apiKey, key }.
# Errors: 400 if the body is malformed JSON.
# NOTE: the Location header is built in the handler but not sent yet
#       (writeJSON receives nil instead of headers).
# See: cmd/api/api_keys.go createAPIKeyHandler
# @name createApiKey
POST {{host}}/v1/api/api-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": 1,
  "description": "API key de prueba",
  "environment": "development",
  "rate_limit_per_minute": 2000
}

### Get API Key by Client ID
# WIP: the handler returns hardcoded test data (ID: 1, "Test Api Key", etc.),
# it does not query the database by client_id yet.
# Path params:
#   id  (int)  client ID, echoed back as client_id in the response
# Returns 200 with { apiKey }.
# Errors: plain-text 404 (http.NotFound) if the ID is not an integer.
# See: cmd/api/api_keys.go getAPIKeyByClientIDHandler
# @name getApiKeyByClientId
GET {{host}}/v1/api/api-key/1
